1
00:00:00,037 --> 00:00:02,166
Helpless Cindy thanks her savior.

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:04,385
Stop. This isn't right.

3
00:00:04,385 --> 00:00:05,711
I need no saving.

4
00:00:05,711 --> 00:00:08,306
We, women, need no saving.

5
00:00:08,306 --> 00:00:10,575
You should have also depicted in this film

6
00:00:10,575 --> 00:00:14,780
that women can defend themselves.

7
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:17,883
Where's the rest of the money
from the transaction in Magallanes?

8
00:00:17,883 --> 00:00:19,584
That's 20 million pesos.

9
00:00:19,584 --> 00:00:22,187
Do you think I forgot about it?

10
00:00:22,187 --> 00:00:23,355
Wait, Congressman!

11
00:00:23,355 --> 00:00:25,291
Hold on!

12
00:00:28,191 --> 00:00:30,026
Why did you even accept this project?

13
00:00:30,026 --> 00:00:32,028
Because I am bound by a contract.

14
00:00:32,028 --> 00:00:34,597
How about you?
Why do you insist on writing a film?

15
00:00:34,597 --> 00:00:37,133
To correct the mistakes I made before.

16
00:00:37,133 --> 00:00:41,571
So if you're telling me
that you're trapped, Joyce...

17
00:00:41,571 --> 00:00:42,973
I mean, Savana.

18
00:00:42,973 --> 00:00:46,476
Let's work together to be free,
and to create a decent output.

19
00:00:46,476 --> 00:00:48,011
Grandpa, how are you?

20
00:00:48,011 --> 00:00:49,546
When did you get out of jail?

21
00:00:49,546 --> 00:00:51,681
Liam dropped the case against me.

22
00:00:51,681 --> 00:00:56,344
And he gave the residents of Verde Village
a livelihood.

23
00:01:09,933 --> 00:01:14,169
My friend, as we all know,

24
00:01:14,169 --> 00:01:19,538
Liam is experiencing trauma
because of the assassination attempt on him.

25
00:01:19,538 --> 00:01:21,632
So I told him to take a break.

26
00:01:21,632 --> 00:01:25,048
May I know how long he will be on break?

27
00:01:25,048 --> 00:01:28,752
I will tell him to come back
as soon as he's okay.

28
00:01:28,752 --> 00:01:34,056
In the meantime, I will manage Casa Fuerte.

29
00:01:36,159 --> 00:01:40,930
Tell your son to recover quickly.

30
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:44,601
Because if not,
his break might become indefinite.

31
00:01:44,601 --> 00:01:47,037
And a gentle reminder...

32
00:01:47,037 --> 00:01:50,774
You are just the face of the company.

33
00:01:50,774 --> 00:01:53,442
A cover-up for my money.

34
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:58,217
We know who's the brain of this company.

35
00:01:58,217 --> 00:02:00,449
And that's Liam.

36
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:05,609
You and Vergil don't have that, my friend.

37
00:02:08,357 --> 00:02:13,896
Make sure he'll come back
to work on my projects.

38
00:02:13,896 --> 00:02:20,736
The longer it takes, the more money I lose.

39
00:02:20,736 --> 00:02:23,639
You might get into debt.

40
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:29,877
You know how I collect my money.

41
00:02:50,932 --> 00:02:57,940
Savana, can you say your line
on page 38, sequence 28?

42
00:03:00,041 --> 00:03:02,311
I won't leave you here.

43
00:03:02,311 --> 00:03:06,148
We'll get out of this cave together,
whether you like it or not.

44
00:03:06,148 --> 00:03:07,749
Why are you so stubborn?

45
00:03:07,749 --> 00:03:08,951
I told you to leave.

46
00:03:08,951 --> 00:03:12,720
I'm not leaving because I love you!

47
00:03:26,535 --> 00:03:31,473
Miss Via, I think being safe is
like living in a dangerous place.

48
00:03:31,473 --> 00:03:34,343
From where we are sitting right now,

49
00:03:34,343 --> 00:03:38,637
I think we're still in a safe space, right?

50
00:03:41,817 --> 00:03:44,589
That's good. Pack up!

51
00:03:46,822 --> 00:03:48,390
Okay, thank you, everyone.

52
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:49,992
Please assist Miss Savana.

53
00:03:49,992 --> 00:03:52,687
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

54
00:03:53,328 --> 00:03:54,797
Hello.

55
00:03:55,831 --> 00:03:58,594
When will you come back?

56
00:04:00,002 --> 00:04:04,072
Of course, we'll have our vacation
when you come back, okay?

57
00:04:04,072 --> 00:04:05,374
I'm done with work, too.

58
00:04:05,374 --> 00:04:08,599
I'll let you know once I get home.

59
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:09,919
Bye.

60
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:12,645
Thank you.

61
00:04:17,185 --> 00:04:18,622
Boss Bro.

62
00:04:18,622 --> 00:04:20,489
Borj, wow, good job.

63
00:04:20,489 --> 00:04:23,025
You came right when the look test was over.

64
00:04:23,025 --> 00:04:24,693
Sorry, Boss Bro.

65
00:04:24,693 --> 00:04:27,529
Ma'am Tess asked me to bring her here.

66
00:04:27,529 --> 00:04:29,064
My mom?

67
00:04:29,064 --> 00:04:31,997
- Where is she?
- She's in the lobby.

68
00:04:33,602 --> 00:04:35,871
By the way, Borj...

69
00:04:35,871 --> 00:04:39,207
You're into show business, right?

70
00:04:39,207 --> 00:04:42,210
A little. Why, Boss Bro?

71
00:04:42,210 --> 00:04:47,115
Do you know if Savana has a boyfriend?

72
00:04:47,115 --> 00:04:49,694
People don't know anything about her

73
00:04:49,694 --> 00:04:51,953
aside from her being vocal
regarding social issues.

74
00:04:51,953 --> 00:04:55,891
But wait, is this still about work?

75
00:04:55,891 --> 00:04:57,092
You're so silly.

76
00:04:57,092 --> 00:04:59,428
- Don't make an issue out of it.
- I'm just asking.

77
00:04:59,428 --> 00:05:00,696
Come on.

78
00:05:00,696 --> 00:05:01,930
Let's go see my mom.

79
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,365
Fine.

80
00:05:05,233 --> 00:05:06,952
Let's go.

81
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:13,108
Hi, Mom!

82
00:05:13,108 --> 00:05:15,280
Hi, Son.

83
00:05:17,713 --> 00:05:19,114
- Hi, Auntie.
- Hello.

84
00:05:19,114 --> 00:05:20,382
Oh, hello.

85
00:05:20,382 --> 00:05:22,417
Savana?

86
00:05:22,417 --> 00:05:23,919
Savana!

87
00:05:23,919 --> 00:05:25,721
Savana.

88
00:05:25,721 --> 00:05:26,788
Hi!

89
00:05:26,788 --> 00:05:28,824
Hello.

90
00:05:28,824 --> 00:05:30,794
My name's Tess.

91
00:05:30,794 --> 00:05:33,128
I am Liam's mom.

92
00:05:33,128 --> 00:05:35,931
- Hi, Aunt Tess.
- Hi, Savana.

93
00:05:35,931 --> 00:05:38,400
I'm your biggest fan.

94
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:41,880
I always watch your TV series,
Captive Hearts.

95
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:45,807
Mom, take it easy.

96
00:05:45,807 --> 00:05:48,310
Auntie, let's go out.

97
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:50,512
Let's have dinner. It's my treat.

98
00:05:50,512 --> 00:05:52,114
Dinner?

99
00:05:52,114 --> 00:05:54,950
I prepared dinner at home.

100
00:05:54,950 --> 00:05:56,518
- Yes.
- Oh.

101
00:05:56,518 --> 00:05:58,314
Yes.

102
00:05:58,314 --> 00:06:00,255
Savana, come with us.

103
00:06:00,255 --> 00:06:02,124
Have dinner with us at home.

104
00:06:02,124 --> 00:06:04,993
Come with us. Let's go?

105
00:06:04,993 --> 00:06:06,465
Come on.

106
00:06:08,397 --> 00:06:10,366
Sure.

107
00:06:10,366 --> 00:06:11,634
Okay.

108
00:06:11,634 --> 00:06:15,204
For real? I'm so thrilled.

109
00:06:15,204 --> 00:06:17,306
Thank you, Savana.

110
00:06:17,306 --> 00:06:19,375
Of course.

111
00:06:19,375 --> 00:06:21,504
Good luck on your dinner date, Boss Bro.

112
00:06:24,213 --> 00:06:27,981
Via, let's just have dinner at home?

113
00:06:29,085 --> 00:06:31,286
Yeah, sure.

114
00:06:32,955 --> 00:06:35,390
Can I bring Queenie?

115
00:06:36,567 --> 00:06:38,260
Sure.

116
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:40,200
Thank you.

117
00:06:45,901 --> 00:06:48,471
I only prepared dinner for three, son.

118
00:06:48,471 --> 00:06:50,438
Just for three people.

119
00:06:51,307 --> 00:06:53,976
But we can have some food delivered. Right?

120
00:06:53,976 --> 00:06:55,444
Yeah, I'll order some food
and have it delivered.

121
00:06:55,444 --> 00:06:56,927
I'll take care of it, Auntie.

122
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,782
- Let's go.
- I can smell trouble.

123
00:06:59,782 --> 00:07:01,150
Come on, Savana.

124
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:02,952
Let's go so you can try my cooking.

125
00:07:02,952 --> 00:07:05,364
Thank you.

126
00:07:10,726 --> 00:07:12,392
Let's go.

127
00:07:23,624 --> 00:07:25,307
Try this, Savana.

128
00:07:25,307 --> 00:07:27,777
This is Liam's second favorite.

129
00:07:27,777 --> 00:07:32,648
My version of kare-kare,
next to my best-seller, adobo.

130
00:07:32,648 --> 00:07:34,683
I love kare-kare, too.

131
00:07:34,683 --> 00:07:36,685
Oh, really? Go ahead.

132
00:07:36,685 --> 00:07:38,720
Eat some more.

133
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,600
Lovely.

134
00:07:39,601 --> 00:07:43,534
This is also your favorite, right, Miss Via?
The kare-kare?

135
00:07:43,534 --> 00:07:45,394
Yes, of course.

136
00:07:45,394 --> 00:07:48,630
Kare-kare is also my favorite, Auntie.

137
00:07:50,132 --> 00:07:51,834
Have some more. Help yourself.

138
00:07:51,834 --> 00:07:52,968
- Mom.
- Don't be shy.

139
00:07:52,968 --> 00:07:55,433
That's enough. She can't eat all of that.

140
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:57,840
It's just a small serving.

141
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,328
- Right?
- Yes, Auntie. Just a little.

142
00:07:59,328 --> 00:08:01,143
I'm on a diet, too.

143
00:08:01,143 --> 00:08:03,309
Oh, dear. Forget about diet.

144
00:08:03,309 --> 00:08:06,482
There's no such thing as diet,
especially when you're here.

145
00:08:06,482 --> 00:08:07,817
What else do you want?

146
00:08:07,817 --> 00:08:09,018
There's shrimp paste.

147
00:08:09,018 --> 00:08:10,019
Here.

148
00:08:10,019 --> 00:08:12,688
- Come on. Put some of this.
- Thank you.

149
00:08:12,688 --> 00:08:13,823
I'm sorry.

150
00:08:13,823 --> 00:08:16,291
My mom is such a big fan of yours.

151
00:08:16,291 --> 00:08:17,526
I know, right?

152
00:08:17,526 --> 00:08:23,065
I love your scene in Captive Hearts.

153
00:08:23,065 --> 00:08:27,036
The one with Anastacia, the villain.

154
00:08:27,036 --> 00:08:28,701
The scene where you said,

155
00:08:28,701 --> 00:08:33,776
"I won't wait for God anymore!
I'll give you your karma!"

156
00:08:33,776 --> 00:08:35,367
Is that right?

157
00:08:35,367 --> 00:08:36,879
Miss Tess is not just a great cook.

158
00:08:36,879 --> 00:08:39,575
She's also a good actress.

159
00:08:41,183 --> 00:08:43,372
Go on, eat.

160
00:08:44,252 --> 00:08:47,289
Wow, looks like she's upstaging you.

161
00:08:47,289 --> 00:08:50,226
It seems that she's auditioning
for the role of daughter-in-law.

162
00:08:50,226 --> 00:08:52,094
The kare-kare is good.

163
00:08:52,094 --> 00:08:53,762
Thank you.

164
00:08:54,396 --> 00:08:56,098
Here is some more.

165
00:08:56,098 --> 00:08:59,568
Auntie, your kare-kare is really good.

166
00:08:59,568 --> 00:09:01,403
What recipe do you use?

167
00:09:01,403 --> 00:09:04,273
Oh, it's a family secret.

168
00:09:05,808 --> 00:09:08,444
But don't worry,
I will teach you how to cook it.

169
00:09:08,444 --> 00:09:10,412
Would you like that?

170
00:09:10,412 --> 00:09:11,914
- Yes.
- Okay, I will.

171
00:09:11,914 --> 00:09:14,650
I will share the recipe to you.

172
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:16,639
Go on and eat.

173
00:09:18,586 --> 00:09:19,937
There.

174
00:09:19,937 --> 00:09:22,000
Thank you, Mom.

175
00:09:29,932 --> 00:09:35,671
Savana, I was surprised
that you still accepted this project.

176
00:09:35,671 --> 00:09:37,740
Why not?

177
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:40,643
Well, I recall from our interview

178
00:09:40,643 --> 00:09:44,934
that you have a strong conviction
against land grabbers.

179
00:09:44,934 --> 00:09:46,410
Isn't it difficult to work

180
00:09:46,411 --> 00:09:49,167
with people with principles
that are different from yours?

181
00:09:49,167 --> 00:09:50,737
Via.

182
00:09:59,696 --> 00:10:05,134
What matters is to be given a second chance
to rectify mistakes.

183
00:10:05,134 --> 00:10:06,870
What do you mean?

184
00:10:06,870 --> 00:10:11,374
If you are referring to Casa Fuerte,

185
00:10:11,374 --> 00:10:13,633
Liam and I already talked.

186
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:17,649
I wouldn't have accepted the movie project.

187
00:10:17,649 --> 00:10:20,188
If he didn't make it up
to the residents of Verde Village.

188
00:10:22,904 --> 00:10:25,297
I didn't know you two were talking.

189
00:10:28,045 --> 00:10:30,680
For the project, of course.

190
00:10:36,798 --> 00:10:38,836
Okay.

191
00:10:38,836 --> 00:10:40,938
For second chances.

192
00:10:40,938 --> 00:10:43,886
That's the theme of the movie, right?

193
00:10:48,378 --> 00:10:50,581
Speaking of changes...

194
00:10:50,581 --> 00:10:54,651
Liam, when can we revise our script?

195
00:10:55,352 --> 00:10:56,920
Do we have to do locked-in writing?

196
00:10:56,920 --> 00:11:00,603
Because if we do,
I have a resort in Tagaytay.

197
00:11:01,603 --> 00:11:03,304
Tagaytay?

198
00:11:05,564 --> 00:11:11,034
How long will you need to be locked-in
to expedite the revision?

199
00:11:11,034 --> 00:11:14,671
It depends on how fast Liam can write.

200
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:18,642
Thank you so much for your offer, Savana.

201
00:11:18,642 --> 00:11:20,611
I'll ask my team.

202
00:11:20,611 --> 00:11:22,079
Great.

203
00:11:22,079 --> 00:11:24,614
Where's your powder room?

204
00:11:25,315 --> 00:11:26,916
Over here.

205
00:11:27,718 --> 00:11:30,119
Thank you. Excuse me.

206
00:11:38,595 --> 00:11:42,165
Love, do you need a locked-in writing?

207
00:11:42,165 --> 00:11:45,969
Well, I suppose
if we have to beat the deadline.

208
00:11:45,969 --> 00:11:47,504
Is it okay with you?

209
00:11:48,739 --> 00:11:50,107
Yeah.

210
00:11:50,107 --> 00:11:51,575
Of course!

211
00:11:51,575 --> 00:11:53,410
Don't worry about me.

212
00:11:53,410 --> 00:11:56,179
Don't worry, I'm okay.

213
00:11:56,179 --> 00:11:58,640
Do what you have to do.

214
00:12:01,318 --> 00:12:03,499
Thank you, Via.

215
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:24,474
Auntie, let me help you wash the dishes.

216
00:12:24,474 --> 00:12:27,177
Oh, you don't have to, darling.

217
00:12:27,177 --> 00:12:28,312
It's okay.

218
00:12:28,312 --> 00:12:30,781
Wait, this is my house.

219
00:12:30,781 --> 00:12:32,382
- Let me do it.
- You're a guest.

220
00:12:32,382 --> 00:12:34,284
No. Just get some rest.

221
00:12:34,284 --> 00:12:35,619
Go on. Relax.

222
00:12:35,619 --> 00:12:37,318
I insist, Auntie.

223
00:12:37,318 --> 00:12:40,477
I want to help. I know how to wash dishes.

224
00:12:40,477 --> 00:12:42,424
Really? For real?

225
00:12:42,424 --> 00:12:43,492
Yes.

226
00:12:43,492 --> 00:12:48,966
We didn't have a housemaid before.

227
00:12:48,966 --> 00:12:53,011
So I always do the dishes.

228
00:12:53,804 --> 00:12:55,539
Now I'm shy.

229
00:12:55,539 --> 00:12:58,642
I'm doing the dishes with a celebrity.

230
00:12:58,642 --> 00:13:00,143
I feel privileged.

231
00:13:00,143 --> 00:13:03,380
Oh, no. Don't think that way.
It's not like that.

232
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,649
No, I got this.

233
00:13:05,649 --> 00:13:06,717
- It's okay...
- I'll do it.

234
00:13:06,717 --> 00:13:08,151
Let me do it, Auntie.

235
00:13:08,151 --> 00:13:10,359
I'm good at washing the dishes.

236
00:13:11,321 --> 00:13:13,824
No. Put it down.

237
00:13:13,824 --> 00:13:17,160
You made me happy today.

238
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:23,066
Super. My heart is full of happiness.

239
00:13:23,066 --> 00:13:26,498
You made me so happy, Savana.

240
00:13:34,878 --> 00:13:37,047
Joyce?

241
00:13:37,047 --> 00:13:39,675
What's the problem?

242
00:13:43,253 --> 00:13:44,855
Nothing, Mom.

243
00:13:44,855 --> 00:13:48,291
The soap got in my eyes.

244
00:13:52,625 --> 00:13:55,594
Tell me the truth.

245
00:13:57,200 --> 00:14:00,136
Did you and Liam fight?

246
00:14:01,976 --> 00:14:05,557
Sometimes, I can't handle Liam anymore.

247
00:14:08,445 --> 00:14:09,880
Mom, why is it like that?

248
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:13,182
Why is he putting his ambition first?

249
00:14:18,055 --> 00:14:22,425
What about me and his son?
Aren't we part of his dreams?

250
00:14:29,433 --> 00:14:33,706
I understand what you feel, my child.

251
00:14:35,839 --> 00:14:43,580
But sometimes, you just have to remind Liam

252
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:47,016
the reason why he's doing things.

253
00:14:48,185 --> 00:14:50,386
Joyce, my dear.

254
00:14:52,823 --> 00:14:56,780
Please, don't give up on Liam. Okay?

255
00:15:16,947 --> 00:15:18,682
Auntie.

256
00:15:18,682 --> 00:15:22,619
Liam! Liam, your mom!

257
00:15:22,619 --> 00:15:23,987
- Mom.
- Liam!

258
00:15:23,987 --> 00:15:25,122
- Mom.
- Auntie, are you okay?

259
00:15:25,122 --> 00:15:26,890
Mom, what's wrong?

260
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:29,059
Borj, please call an ambulance.

261
00:15:29,059 --> 00:15:30,293
Oh my God! What happened?

262
00:15:30,293 --> 00:15:32,462
- Savana!
- I don't know.

263
00:15:32,462 --> 00:15:35,632
We were just washing the dishes
when she got dizzy.

264
00:15:35,632 --> 00:15:37,067
Mom, are you okay?

265
00:15:37,067 --> 00:15:39,469
Get me some water, please. I'm okay.

266
00:15:39,469 --> 00:15:40,837
I'm fine. I just got dizzy.

267
00:15:40,837 --> 00:15:42,960
Are you sure? I'm afraid it's...

268
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,774
No, son.

269
00:15:45,909 --> 00:15:49,079
No. Don't overreact. I just got dizzy.

270
00:15:49,079 --> 00:15:51,648
I just got excited.

271
00:15:51,648 --> 00:15:54,317
I was just so excited to be with Savana.

272
00:15:54,317 --> 00:15:55,385
- Are you sure?
- Auntie...

273
00:15:55,385 --> 00:15:57,320
Yes.

274
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:00,557
Get some rest for now. We'll do the cleaning.

275
00:16:00,557 --> 00:16:02,223
No, no. That would be embarrassing.

276
00:16:02,223 --> 00:16:04,196
- I'm okay.
- Auntie, do you want to get some fresh air?

277
00:16:04,196 --> 00:16:06,487
I'll go with you.

278
00:16:11,535 --> 00:16:12,836
Okay.

279
00:16:12,836 --> 00:16:14,971
Okay, let's go.

280
00:16:31,721 --> 00:16:38,272
Savana, why did you order our caretaker
to prepare the resort in Tagaytay?

281
00:16:39,129 --> 00:16:41,731
Savana, I'll just bring your stuff
to your room.

282
00:16:41,731 --> 00:16:43,866
Excuse me, Madam.

283
00:16:47,137 --> 00:16:48,805
Yes, Mommy.

284
00:16:48,805 --> 00:16:54,844
We need it for our locked-in writing
at Blacksmith.

285
00:16:56,980 --> 00:17:00,049
Is Liam going to join?

286
00:17:00,984 --> 00:17:02,881
Is he coming?

287
00:17:02,881 --> 00:17:05,047
Yes, because he's the creative manager.

288
00:17:05,047 --> 00:17:09,292
Tell Liam that he's very much welcome
at our resort.

289
00:17:09,292 --> 00:17:13,263
I will have the biggest suite
ready for the two of you.

290
00:17:13,263 --> 00:17:14,931
What?

291
00:17:14,931 --> 00:17:20,470
You didn't tell me Liam made headlines

292
00:17:20,470 --> 00:17:24,841
because he's an heir
of the Herrera Group of Companies.

293
00:17:24,841 --> 00:17:27,877
I didn't know he was rich.

294
00:17:30,034 --> 00:17:32,929
And so what, Mom?

295
00:17:32,929 --> 00:17:35,151
You should get close to him.

296
00:17:35,151 --> 00:17:37,087
Work on it.

297
00:17:37,087 --> 00:17:39,055
That's what I mean.

298
00:17:41,958 --> 00:17:44,453
You are unbelievable, Mom.

299
00:17:45,459 --> 00:17:48,431
Mom, you're hurting me!

300
00:17:48,431 --> 00:17:50,867
Let's make it clear.

301
00:17:50,867 --> 00:17:56,439
Why did you accept such a cheap movie
if you're not interested in Liam?

302
00:17:56,439 --> 00:17:59,608
You have a lot of better offers.

303
00:18:00,343 --> 00:18:03,546
What do you take me for, Mom?

304
00:18:03,546 --> 00:18:07,450
A product that you can sell to just anyone?

305
00:18:08,518 --> 00:18:11,021
I'm doing the project in Blacksmith

306
00:18:11,021 --> 00:18:16,993
because they listen to me
instead of controlling me.

307
00:18:16,993 --> 00:18:19,329
What are you trying to say?
That I am controlling you?

308
00:18:19,329 --> 00:18:21,997
Is that what you mean? Is that it?

309
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:27,537
I worked hard for your career.

310
00:18:27,537 --> 00:18:32,042
I won't let you ruin it!

311
00:18:32,042 --> 00:18:36,559
And I won't let us go back to being poor.

312
00:19:01,938 --> 00:19:05,086
My mom is the worst.

313
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:12,867
I did everything she wanted.

314
00:19:14,117 --> 00:19:17,245
I always do what she wants.

315
00:19:18,621 --> 00:19:20,757
Everything.

316
00:19:20,757 --> 00:19:23,565
Everything she wants.

317
00:19:25,061 --> 00:19:29,365
But why can't she give me a little space?

318
00:19:32,702 --> 00:19:34,871
- Savana...
- Even just a little respect.

319
00:19:34,871 --> 00:19:37,073
Savana, that's enough. You're already drunk.

320
00:19:37,073 --> 00:19:39,706
- You should stop.
- I'm not drunk yet.

321
00:19:41,745 --> 00:19:44,370
You're not drunk yet, too.

322
00:19:45,248 --> 00:19:47,317
- Savana, that's enough.
- Let's drink some more.

323
00:19:47,317 --> 00:19:48,585
Cheers!

324
00:19:48,585 --> 00:19:51,388
Savana, you've had enough.

325
00:19:51,388 --> 00:19:52,789
No.

326
00:19:52,789 --> 00:19:54,758
Cheers, Tristan. Join me.

327
00:19:54,758 --> 00:19:56,892
I need to drink.

328
00:19:58,795 --> 00:20:00,789
Please? Cheers.

329
00:20:03,433 --> 00:20:05,502
That's enough, Savana.

330
00:20:05,502 --> 00:20:07,102
You know what...

331
00:20:09,139 --> 00:20:15,128
People think that life is all good
when you're a celebrity.

332
00:20:17,113 --> 00:20:19,416
But no!

333
00:20:19,416 --> 00:20:21,951
They don't know about the pressure.

334
00:20:21,951 --> 00:20:24,454
Okay. Let's go. That's enough.
I'll drive you home.

335
00:20:24,454 --> 00:20:26,856
- Let's go.
- No.

336
00:20:26,856 --> 00:20:28,458
- I don't want to go home yet.
- Savana, stop.

337
00:20:28,458 --> 00:20:29,959
- Tonight...
- Savana, that's enough.

338
00:20:29,959 --> 00:20:31,194
I'll have fun tonight.

339
00:20:31,194 --> 00:20:33,963
Because it's the first time
that I get to go out.

340
00:20:33,963 --> 00:20:35,865
Savana, enough.

341
00:20:35,865 --> 00:20:37,200
Let's go. I'll drive you home.

342
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:40,002
- Come on.
- I said no!

343
00:20:42,939 --> 00:20:44,474
Savana, that's enough!

344
00:20:44,474 --> 00:20:45,475
Savana!

345
00:20:45,475 --> 00:20:47,811
- Waiter, one more round, please.
- What's going on?

346
00:20:47,811 --> 00:20:50,114
Maxine.

347
00:20:50,114 --> 00:20:51,879
Savana's drunk already.

348
00:20:51,879 --> 00:20:53,884
She doesn't want to go home.

349
00:20:53,884 --> 00:20:56,954
- I have an early call time tomorrow.
- Do you have to go?

350
00:20:56,954 --> 00:21:00,157
Go. We'll take care of Savana.

351
00:21:00,157 --> 00:21:02,159
Thank you, Maxine. I owe you one.

352
00:21:02,159 --> 00:21:04,561
- Please take care of Savana.
- Sure.

353
00:21:04,561 --> 00:21:06,732
- Savana.
- Take care.

354
00:21:11,735 --> 00:21:13,736
Hi, girls!

355
00:21:27,576 --> 00:21:31,779
Via, do we have a problem?

356
00:21:34,195 --> 00:21:36,830
Is there something I should be worried about?

357
00:21:41,131 --> 00:21:46,936
What is this about?
Is this about the unexpected dinner with Mom?

358
00:21:47,897 --> 00:21:51,341
Via, I'm sorry. I'll make it up to you.

359
00:21:54,676 --> 00:21:57,179
That's where you're good at.

360
00:21:57,179 --> 00:21:59,437
Second chances.

361
00:22:03,852 --> 00:22:07,422
Are you jealous of Savana?

362
00:22:09,558 --> 00:22:14,463
Why didn't you tell me
you're in constant communication with her?

363
00:22:14,463 --> 00:22:18,734
Via, she's my actor. We're making a film.

364
00:22:18,734 --> 00:22:21,406
I thought you understood.

365
00:22:22,237 --> 00:22:24,573
Via, I need to save this project.

366
00:22:24,573 --> 00:22:26,687
I need to appease her.

367
00:22:29,845 --> 00:22:32,414
I'm sorry.

368
00:22:32,414 --> 00:22:35,680
Maybe I just have a lot on my mind.

369
00:22:39,488 --> 00:22:41,055
It's okay, Love.

370
00:22:42,257 --> 00:22:43,922
I'm sorry, too.

371
00:22:45,494 --> 00:22:47,195
I love you.

372
00:23:06,114 --> 00:23:08,839
Girls, let's dance.

373
00:23:14,756 --> 00:23:17,225
Chanel, take a video.

374
00:23:19,928 --> 00:23:22,631
You know what, guys...

375
00:23:22,631 --> 00:23:25,131
My mom is like this.

376
00:23:25,912 --> 00:23:27,935
Savana...

377
00:23:28,936 --> 00:23:32,606
Savana, act more convincingly.

378
00:23:32,606 --> 00:23:35,509
Savana, you're overacting.

379
00:23:35,509 --> 00:23:38,111
Savana, you should cry!

380
00:23:38,111 --> 00:23:39,158
Savana.

381
00:23:39,158 --> 00:23:43,250
Savana, you should only
shed tears in your left eye.

382
00:23:43,250 --> 00:23:44,618
Savana, wait!

383
00:23:44,618 --> 00:23:46,920
Don't eat that, Savana!

384
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:49,539
You're so fat already!

385
00:23:58,365 --> 00:24:01,277
This is so hard.

386
00:24:04,416 --> 00:24:08,152
I can't make decisions for myself!

387
00:24:10,577 --> 00:24:12,986
I don't want this anymore.

388
00:24:14,889 --> 00:24:18,759
Our friend gets drunk so easily.

389
00:24:21,423 --> 00:24:24,526
Really, Savana?

390
00:24:24,526 --> 00:24:29,998
Who's so controlling?

391
00:24:29,998 --> 00:24:32,294
- Who's controlling?
- Who else?

392
00:24:33,126 --> 00:24:38,206
My mom is controlling.

393
00:24:38,206 --> 00:24:41,943
She's a terror manager.

394
00:24:43,178 --> 00:24:46,114
- OMG, girls. This is so juicy.
- I'm getting tired of it.

395
00:24:46,114 --> 00:24:48,347
Just continue recording it.

396
00:24:57,659 --> 00:25:01,449
I can't make decisions for myself!

397
00:25:08,370 --> 00:25:11,421
Our friend can't handle alcohol.

398
00:25:12,641 --> 00:25:14,976
Really, Savana?

399
00:25:14,976 --> 00:25:17,343
Who's so controlling?

400
00:25:18,313 --> 00:25:20,048
Who's controlling?

401
00:25:20,048 --> 00:25:22,038
Who else?

402
00:25:22,788 --> 00:25:27,989
My mom, who's a terror manager...

403
00:25:27,989 --> 00:25:30,959
She is so controlling.

404
00:25:30,959 --> 00:25:33,266
Are you recording this?
Make sure you're doing it right.

405
00:25:33,266 --> 00:25:35,538
I'm like...

406
00:25:37,685 --> 00:25:40,221
I'm like a goldfish.

407
00:25:41,236 --> 00:25:43,672
I'm like a goldfish. Like...

408
00:25:49,645 --> 00:25:52,514
Can you imagine a goldfish?

409
00:25:52,514 --> 00:25:54,603
Goldfish.

410
00:25:56,158 --> 00:26:06,428
I'm like a goldfish in a very tiny aquarium.

411
00:26:06,428 --> 00:26:09,864
What does a goldfish look like again?

412
00:26:16,226 --> 00:26:19,734
- So that's what a goldfish looks like.
- That's a goldfish.

413
00:26:22,515 --> 00:26:27,115
Why won't she just flush me in the toilet?

414
00:26:30,719 --> 00:26:32,120
It's so messy. Sorry.

415
00:26:32,120 --> 00:26:34,174
Yeah.

416
00:26:40,295 --> 00:26:42,167
Are you okay?

417
00:26:43,021 --> 00:26:44,799
Yes.

418
00:26:44,799 --> 00:26:46,801
I'm okay.

419
00:26:54,676 --> 00:26:57,888
What the heck!
Are you really throwing up here?

420
00:27:00,982 --> 00:27:04,183
I was just kidding. I'm still okay.
Look, I can still dance.

421
00:27:11,727 --> 00:27:14,685
I don't want to go home yet.

422
00:27:14,685 --> 00:27:18,367
- Party, party!
- Come on, Savana!

423
00:27:18,367 --> 00:27:20,102
Let's go.

424
00:27:20,102 --> 00:27:22,571
I don't want to go home yet.

425
00:27:22,571 --> 00:27:24,106
Let's go back.

426
00:27:24,106 --> 00:27:26,175
- Let's go back!
- No!

427
00:27:26,175 --> 00:27:28,177
I'm not enjoying it anymore, so let's go.

428
00:27:28,177 --> 00:27:31,268
Maxine, I'm still having a good time.

429
00:27:32,281 --> 00:27:34,917
I'm still having fun, so let's go.

430
00:27:34,917 --> 00:27:36,685
- Let's go back.
- She's so hopeless.

431
00:27:36,685 --> 00:27:39,855
What do we do?
Are we going to leave Savana here?

432
00:27:39,855 --> 00:27:42,057
- She asked for it.
- Are you sure?

433
00:27:42,057 --> 00:27:43,959
You can stay with her if you want.
Stay with her.

434
00:27:43,959 --> 00:27:45,961
No, let's go.

435
00:27:45,961 --> 00:27:47,565
Come on, let's go.

436
00:27:48,631 --> 00:27:50,549
Hey!

437
00:27:57,504 --> 00:27:59,909
Isn't she a celebrity?

438
00:27:59,909 --> 00:28:01,143
Come on, bro.

439
00:28:01,143 --> 00:28:02,636
That's Savana.

440
00:28:02,636 --> 00:28:04,179
Savana?

441
00:28:04,878 --> 00:28:05,966
Savana!

442
00:28:05,966 --> 00:28:06,815
- Who are you...
- Want to come with us?

443
00:28:06,815 --> 00:28:08,284
Why are you grabbing me?

444
00:28:08,284 --> 00:28:11,153
- Let's have fun.
- Let go of me!

445
00:28:11,153 --> 00:28:13,656
- Join us.
- Let go...

446
00:28:16,559 --> 00:28:18,733
How dare you!

447
00:28:21,764 --> 00:28:23,157
Get her!

448
00:28:26,268 --> 00:28:28,337
Help!

449
00:28:28,337 --> 00:28:30,139
Come with us!

450
00:28:30,139 --> 00:28:32,341
Help!

451
00:28:32,341 --> 00:28:34,408
Let go of me!

452
00:28:34,408 --> 00:28:35,945
Help me, please!

453
00:28:35,945 --> 00:28:37,513
Help me!

454
00:28:37,513 --> 00:28:39,302
Help!

455
00:28:40,349 --> 00:28:41,483
Help!

456
00:28:41,483 --> 00:28:43,018
Help!

457
00:28:43,018 --> 00:28:44,453
- Love!
- Savana!

458
00:28:44,453 --> 00:28:46,536
- Liam!
- Leave her alone!

459
00:28:48,457 --> 00:28:49,525
Love...

460
00:28:49,525 --> 00:28:51,126
Oh my God, Savana.

461
00:28:51,126 --> 00:28:52,695
Savana!

462
00:29:01,837 --> 00:29:04,122
Get in! Get in the car.

463
00:29:33,502 --> 00:29:34,931
Hey!

464
00:29:55,557 --> 00:29:56,991
Hey!

465
00:30:05,768 --> 00:30:07,069
Love...

466
00:30:07,069 --> 00:30:09,505
- Are you guys okay?
- Liam.

467
00:30:09,505 --> 00:30:11,486
Who are they?

468
00:30:19,448 --> 00:30:21,441
- Careful with her head.
- Yeah.

469
00:30:33,195 --> 00:30:35,764
I'll get some cold water and a towel.

470
00:30:35,764 --> 00:30:37,125
Okay.

471
00:30:55,484 --> 00:30:57,206
Joyce...

472
00:31:04,660 --> 00:31:07,042
What were you doing?

473
00:31:09,098 --> 00:31:11,906
Why are you getting drunk?

474
00:31:13,235 --> 00:31:17,436
When we were still together
back in the old world,

475
00:31:21,744 --> 00:31:25,475
you didn't even take a sip of alcohol.

476
00:31:27,249 --> 00:31:29,852
<i>I want you to meet Liam, my boyfriend.</i>

477
00:31:29,852 --> 00:31:31,253
Liam Herrera.

478
00:31:31,253 --> 00:31:32,468
You know each other?

479
00:31:32,468 --> 00:31:34,523
He was at my filming the other day.

480
00:31:34,523 --> 00:31:38,460
You didn't tell me that you know each other.

481
00:31:38,460 --> 00:31:41,947
Auntie, your kare-kare is so good.

482
00:31:41,947 --> 00:31:43,866
What recipe do you use?

483
00:31:43,866 --> 00:31:47,636
Oh, it's a family secret.

484
00:31:47,636 --> 00:31:50,205
But don't worry.
I'll share my recipe with you, Savana.

485
00:31:50,205 --> 00:31:51,657
Would you like that?

486
00:31:51,657 --> 00:31:53,709
- Yes, sure.
- Okay, I will.

487
00:31:53,709 --> 00:31:56,444
I will give you the recipe.

488
00:32:16,231 --> 00:32:17,733
Love...

489
00:32:19,735 --> 00:32:22,404
Can you give us some privacy for now?

490
00:32:22,404 --> 00:32:24,772
I'll just give Savana a sponge bath.

491
00:32:28,972 --> 00:32:30,401
Sure.

492
00:33:18,860 --> 00:33:20,462
I won't leave you here.

493
00:33:20,462 --> 00:33:23,565
We'll get out of this cave together,
whether you like it or not.

494
00:33:23,565 --> 00:33:25,033
Why are you so stubborn?

495
00:33:25,033 --> 00:33:26,235
I said, go.

496
00:33:26,235 --> 00:33:30,371
I'm not going anywhere because I love you!

497
00:34:03,472 --> 00:34:05,882
I saw the way you look at her.

498
00:34:09,529 --> 00:34:12,179
What do you mean?

499
00:34:22,326 --> 00:34:24,919
I saw the way you look at her.

500
00:34:30,499 --> 00:34:33,000
Liam, I'm a woman, too.

501
00:34:34,536 --> 00:34:39,440
I know how a man looks at me
when he likes me.

502
00:34:42,744 --> 00:34:45,313
Are you jealous of Savana?

503
00:34:55,757 --> 00:34:57,778
Please...

504
00:35:01,699 --> 00:35:08,105
Forget about whatever you are feeling
right now.

505
00:35:11,810 --> 00:35:14,849
I will also pretend
that this conversation never happened.

506
00:35:22,084 --> 00:35:23,892
I love you.

507
00:35:27,756 --> 00:35:30,424
I love you so much.

508
00:36:13,702 --> 00:36:15,461
Sorry.

509
00:36:17,751 --> 00:36:19,483
Breakfast?

510
00:36:26,709 --> 00:36:28,517
How are you feeling?

511
00:36:28,517 --> 00:36:30,484
Are you okay now?

512
00:36:35,190 --> 00:36:37,124
Have some coffee...

513
00:36:37,959 --> 00:36:40,528
To cure your hangover.

514
00:36:42,364 --> 00:36:45,032
Sorry, why are you here?

515
00:36:46,401 --> 00:36:48,078
This is my condo.

516
00:36:48,970 --> 00:36:52,820
Sorry, don't you remember anything
about what happened?

517
00:36:54,643 --> 00:36:58,046
You almost got yourself in danger, Savana.

518
00:36:58,046 --> 00:37:00,882
Good thing Liam and I passed by.

519
00:37:03,318 --> 00:37:05,180
I'm sorry.

520
00:37:06,922 --> 00:37:10,759
I'm sorry. Please tell Liam, I'm sorry.

521
00:37:10,759 --> 00:37:12,527
This is so embarrassing.

522
00:37:12,527 --> 00:37:14,329
Oh, dear. Sorry.

523
00:37:14,329 --> 00:37:16,832
Please tell him I'm sorry.
This really is embarrassing.

524
00:37:16,832 --> 00:37:20,401
- I'm so sorry.
- It's okay. Don't worry about it.

525
00:37:28,543 --> 00:37:33,615
Savana, if you need someone to talk to...

526
00:37:33,615 --> 00:37:35,583
I'm here, okay?

527
00:37:37,167 --> 00:37:42,305
I'm sure I'm better company than alcohol.

528
00:37:50,999 --> 00:37:52,267
I'll leave you for now.

529
00:37:52,267 --> 00:37:53,774
Go, eat.

530
00:37:54,803 --> 00:37:56,037
I should leave.

531
00:37:56,037 --> 00:37:58,874
Go on, eat breakfast first.

532
00:37:58,874 --> 00:38:01,905
I'll give you your privacy. Go ahead.

533
00:38:03,445 --> 00:38:05,947
I'm like a goldfish.

534
00:38:08,817 --> 00:38:11,386
She's so controlling.

535
00:38:11,386 --> 00:38:18,897
My mom, who's a terror manager,
is so controlling.

536
00:38:39,548 --> 00:38:41,216
What is this, Savana?

537
00:38:41,216 --> 00:38:44,452
What kind of life choices
have you been making?

538
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:50,748
What am I doing to myself?

539
00:39:29,267 --> 00:39:33,601
[A Thousand Miles Skin Care]

540
00:39:39,425 --> 00:39:41,927
It's too early in the day to be frowning.

541
00:39:41,929 --> 00:39:43,686
That's bad luck.

542
00:39:52,242 --> 00:39:54,989
Do you want to eat?

543
00:39:55,824 --> 00:39:57,133
Yes.

544
00:39:57,906 --> 00:39:59,727
Okay. Then, let's go.

545
00:40:08,069 --> 00:40:10,705
Bro, I'm just curious.

546
00:40:10,705 --> 00:40:14,576
You are either mad or lonely
whenever you pass by this place.

547
00:40:14,576 --> 00:40:16,877
Is it because of that billboard?

548
00:40:19,089 --> 00:40:24,531
There are things in the past
that I want to change.

549
00:40:24,531 --> 00:40:25,601
Decisions I made

550
00:40:25,601 --> 00:40:30,324
that I should have thought about
more carefully.

551
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:33,695
If only I knew the repercussions...

552
00:40:33,695 --> 00:40:37,699
Bro! You're still in control of your life.

553
00:40:37,699 --> 00:40:39,534
You can't bring back the past,

554
00:40:39,534 --> 00:40:44,004
but you can make the right choices
for the people you love.

555
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:47,809
What if I want to bring back
the people whom I lost?

556
00:40:47,809 --> 00:40:51,679
Have you asked yourself
if they want to be back in your life?

557
00:40:52,667 --> 00:40:56,384
- That's some serious talk.
- Yes... Real talk, bro.

558
00:40:56,384 --> 00:40:58,277
Do you know why you're having a hard time?

559
00:40:58,277 --> 00:40:59,988
Why?

560
00:40:59,988 --> 00:41:03,691
You can't stand by what makes you happy.

561
00:41:14,135 --> 00:41:17,038
Girl, you're driving me nuts.
You didn't come home last night.

562
00:41:17,038 --> 00:41:18,573
I stayed up late waiting for you.

563
00:41:18,573 --> 00:41:20,875
But don't worry, I took care of your mom.

564
00:41:20,875 --> 00:41:22,110
We look like each other, anyway.

565
00:41:22,110 --> 00:41:24,713
I will just send your stuff to the resort.

566
00:41:24,713 --> 00:41:26,981
Be safe. Take care, okay?

567
00:41:26,981 --> 00:41:28,449
Bye.

568
00:41:37,659 --> 00:41:39,494
- Smile!
- Picture, picture!

569
00:41:39,494 --> 00:41:41,996
- Guys, selfie!
- Wacky!

570
00:41:41,996 --> 00:41:44,199
They won't stop taking pictures.

571
00:41:44,199 --> 00:41:45,633
I know.

572
00:41:45,633 --> 00:41:47,936
Doesn't she have a road manager?

573
00:41:47,936 --> 00:41:50,905
Let her be. She likes it.

574
00:41:53,747 --> 00:41:56,375
Welcome to our resort.

575
00:41:56,375 --> 00:41:58,878
OMG! The food is overflowing!
We're going to eat.

576
00:41:58,878 --> 00:42:00,153
We're going to swim.

577
00:42:00,153 --> 00:42:01,794
- Swim?
- Just give me time.

578
00:42:01,794 --> 00:42:04,411
- Are we on vacation?
- Yes, Borj.

579
00:42:04,411 --> 00:42:07,188
Are we here to work or to have fun??

580
00:42:09,652 --> 00:42:11,693
Why, Liam?

581
00:42:11,693 --> 00:42:13,360
Are we going straight to work?

582
00:42:15,361 --> 00:42:17,370
Okay, fine.

583
00:42:17,370 --> 00:42:18,839
You can swim.

584
00:42:19,862 --> 00:42:21,903
- Let's go!
- Come on, hurry up!

585
00:42:21,903 --> 00:42:25,097
- You're too excited.
- Be careful.

586
00:42:29,408 --> 00:42:31,089
Oh, wow.

587
00:42:31,089 --> 00:42:34,136
He came prepared.

588
00:42:34,136 --> 00:42:35,517
He really came prepared.

589
00:42:35,517 --> 00:42:37,952
Hey!

590
00:42:37,952 --> 00:42:42,889
- Come on!
- Later. I still have to work.

591
00:42:42,889 --> 00:42:44,144
It's cold.

592
00:42:44,144 --> 00:42:45,667
Go, Deedee!

593
00:42:46,995 --> 00:42:48,794
What?

594
00:42:48,794 --> 00:42:51,042
Go, Deedee!

595
00:42:58,974 --> 00:43:01,014
Go, fight!

596
00:43:14,279 --> 00:43:16,425
All right!

597
00:43:17,826 --> 00:43:20,527
Get your drinks.

598
00:43:22,730 --> 00:43:24,265
Can you please hand me that?

599
00:43:24,265 --> 00:43:25,733
Go ahead.

600
00:43:25,733 --> 00:43:27,268
Can I have some grapes?

601
00:43:27,268 --> 00:43:30,171
That's good.

602
00:43:30,171 --> 00:43:33,739
This one... Try this one.

603
00:43:33,739 --> 00:43:35,907
Yeah, this is good.

604
00:43:44,352 --> 00:43:46,321
The action scenes won't be a problem.

605
00:43:46,321 --> 00:43:50,573
A reluctant hero who got branded
as a traitor by the community

606
00:43:50,573 --> 00:43:53,033
because of a single mistake.

607
00:43:53,033 --> 00:43:54,529
- But...
- The hero's objective

608
00:43:54,529 --> 00:43:59,099
is to make up for the wrong
he did to the woman he loves.

609
00:44:00,768 --> 00:44:06,107
He can't tell her that it was his fault
that her family died.

610
00:44:06,107 --> 00:44:11,012
So, should the movie end with their breakup?

611
00:44:11,012 --> 00:44:16,077
It's enough that he paid for his sins
by saving the whole community.

612
00:44:16,077 --> 00:44:18,398
But he doesn't get the girl in the end.

613
00:44:19,109 --> 00:44:22,290
If you were to ask me, the hero should die.

614
00:44:22,290 --> 00:44:26,294
That's his biggest redemption.
Sacrificing his life.

615
00:44:26,294 --> 00:44:28,997
That's me. Why would you kill me?

616
00:44:28,997 --> 00:44:30,890
That will make you a hero.

617
00:44:30,890 --> 00:44:32,667
It's morbid, though.

618
00:44:32,667 --> 00:44:35,837
And then maybe they can be reincarnated.

619
00:44:35,837 --> 00:44:39,407
They will meet at a different time.

620
00:44:39,407 --> 00:44:43,110
Deedee,
I think that's a different film already.

621
00:44:44,145 --> 00:44:46,210
What do you think, Boss Bro?

622
00:44:49,050 --> 00:44:52,186
I think they should end up together.

623
00:44:52,186 --> 00:44:55,085
Right. A happy ending.

624
00:44:57,825 --> 00:44:59,905
Like how, Liam?

625
00:45:03,598 --> 00:45:06,960
He will confess to her everything.

626
00:45:08,169 --> 00:45:10,271
He'll pay for his sins.

627
00:45:10,271 --> 00:45:13,508
He'll take in all of the woman's anger.

628
00:45:13,508 --> 00:45:15,177
But in the process,

629
00:45:15,177 --> 00:45:17,233
the girl will see

630
00:45:17,234 --> 00:45:22,232
how much effort the man puts
into changing his ways.

631
00:45:25,219 --> 00:45:29,123
After all,
that's what our movie is all about.

632
00:45:29,123 --> 00:45:31,669
It's about second chances.

633
00:45:40,508 --> 00:45:43,310
Excuse me. I have to take this call.

634
00:45:46,975 --> 00:45:48,592
Hello?

635
00:47:59,949 --> 00:48:01,823
Oh my, a crocodile!

636
00:48:03,940 --> 00:48:06,465
Sorry, Savana.

637
00:48:06,465 --> 00:48:08,026
Liam.

638
00:48:10,485 --> 00:48:12,451
I'm sorry, Savana.

639
00:48:12,451 --> 00:48:16,325
I went swimming
so I won't have to swim with the others.

640
00:48:19,498 --> 00:48:21,316
Actually, that's what I have in mind, too.

641
00:48:27,426 --> 00:48:31,753
Savana, if you don't mind...

642
00:48:35,510 --> 00:48:38,346
What really happened?

643
00:48:38,346 --> 00:48:41,256
Why did you get drunk the other night?

644
00:48:47,021 --> 00:48:49,824
Sorry if I have invaded your privacy...

645
00:48:49,824 --> 00:48:51,342
It's okay.

646
00:48:52,219 --> 00:48:55,287
You have the right to ask.

647
00:48:56,197 --> 00:48:58,833
You saved me.

648
00:48:58,833 --> 00:49:01,335
Don't worry about that.

649
00:49:02,036 --> 00:49:04,504
I don't know, Liam.

650
00:49:05,682 --> 00:49:08,673
I know I wanted this.

651
00:49:09,710 --> 00:49:15,515
Many will do everything
to get to where I am right now.

652
00:49:18,152 --> 00:49:21,680
But I feel like I'm a robot.

653
00:49:24,192 --> 00:49:26,027
A robot that is being controlled.

654
00:49:26,027 --> 00:49:28,062
"Savana, do this."

655
00:49:28,062 --> 00:49:29,430
"Act like this... Cry like that."

656
00:49:29,430 --> 00:49:31,732
"You can't make a mistake!"

657
00:49:32,567 --> 00:49:34,402
You're brave.

658
00:49:34,402 --> 00:49:37,139
Why are you letting them control you?

659
00:49:38,573 --> 00:49:41,053
What made you say that I'm brave?

660
00:49:43,444 --> 00:49:49,025
You defended the residents of Verde Village
from me, remember?

661
00:49:49,917 --> 00:49:52,886
Why can't you defend yourself?

662
00:50:00,674 --> 00:50:04,444
Maybe that's how I deal
with all my anger towards this world...

663
00:50:05,510 --> 00:50:07,869
Through my advocacies.

664
00:50:12,940 --> 00:50:14,898
Savana...

665
00:50:16,058 --> 00:50:20,547
I hope you use the bravery you've shown me

666
00:50:22,750 --> 00:50:28,328
to fight for your own happiness.

667
00:50:36,831 --> 00:50:39,445
I still need to muster enough courage.

668
00:51:00,489 --> 00:51:02,106
Via.

669
00:51:14,802 --> 00:51:17,838
I was about to text you
that this is my mom's treat.

670
00:51:17,838 --> 00:51:20,006
Don't worry. I can deal with your mom.

671
00:51:20,006 --> 00:51:22,908
He's the reason why my dreams for you
got ruined.

672
00:51:22,908 --> 00:51:26,178
Everything that has happened to us
is because of our choices.

673
00:51:26,178 --> 00:51:28,100
Joyce...

674
00:51:30,303 --> 00:51:31,740
Joyce.

675
00:51:31,740 --> 00:51:35,489
- We should kill the hero.
- Right. Because he's a traitor.

676
00:51:35,489 --> 00:51:38,865
Disloyal and unfaithful.

677
00:51:38,865 --> 00:51:42,756
Even I could kill that man.

678
00:51:42,756 --> 00:51:46,433
Actually, he and his mistress.

679
00:51:50,736 --> 00:51:56,175
This story should have a magical typewriter.

680
00:51:56,175 --> 00:52:00,212
Savana! I said this story should have magic.

681
00:52:00,212 --> 00:52:05,829
They got separated
because of that magical typewriter.

682
00:52:05,829 --> 00:52:08,255
Maybe her non-showbiz boyfriend.
